  The deploy service is not set up yet. It rolls out and updates your stacks and
  runs a╔═ Deploy service ═════════════════════════════════════════════╗to      
  Docker║ ⚠ Set up the deploy service now?                             ║etup    
        ║                                                              ║        
        ║ It creates the system user qhost-deploy in the group docker, ║        
        ║ its channel and its unit, and starts the service. The host   ║        
        ║ service gets no access to Docker. These steps run as root:   ║        
        ║ $ groupadd --system qhost-deploy                             ║        
        ║ $ useradd --system --gid qhost-deploy --no-create-home       ║        
        ║   --home-dir /var/lib/qhost-deploy --shell /usr/sbin/nologin ║        
        ║   qhost-deploy                                               ║        
        ║ $ usermod --append --groups docker qhost-deploy              ║        
        ║ $ systemctl enable --now qhost-deploy                        ║        
        ║ $ sudo qhost deploy-service setup --confirm --yes --output   ║        
        ║   json                                                       ║        
        ║                                                              ║        
        ║ [ yes, with sudo ]  > cancel <                               ║        
        ║ y yes, with sudo  n/esc/enter cancel                         ║        
